- # `↯/s.106.3` — `Json.Provider.Error`
+ # `↯/s.106.3` — `Json.Provider.Error`

- Raised when a JSON value does not satisfy the schema it is being
- validated against.
+ Se lanza cuando un valor JSON no satisface el esquema con el que se está validando.

- ## Cause
+ ## Causa

- Jacinta's `Json.Provider` validates JSON values against a schema as a record's fields are read,
- and reports each mismatch via this error, through the `Tactic` of the code reading the field, so
- that a validating reader can collect them all. The message is `the
- JSON was not valid according to the schema because $reason`.
+ El `Json.Provider` de Jacinta valida los valores JSON contra un esquema a medida que se leen los
+ campos de un registro, e informa de cada discrepancia mediante este error, a través de la
+ `Tactic` del código que lee el campo, para que un lector que valida pueda reunirlas todas. El
+ mensaje es `the JSON was not valid according to the schema because $reason`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Code
- column  Reason
- column  Meaning
- column  Message
- column  Resolution
- row  `↯/s.106.3.1`  `JsonType`  The value's type does not match what the schema requires.  `[↯/s.106.3.1] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because expected JSON type number, but found string`  Provide a value of the type the schema requires, or relax the schema if the type is genuinely flexible.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.2`  `MissingValue`  A required value is absent from the JSON. The reason names the missing field where it is known.  `[↯/s.106.3.2] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value of locality was missing`  Add the missing field, or mark it optional in the schema.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.3`  `IntOutOfRange`  An integer value falls outside the `minimum`/`maximum` allowed by the schema. Raised by the `"integer!"` provider type; an absent bound is `Unset` rather than a sentinel.  `[↯/s.106.3.3] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value was not between 1 and 99`  Constrain the value to the schema's permitted range.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.4`  `PatternMismatch`  A string value does not match the regular expression in the schema's `pattern`.  `[↯/s.106.3.4] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value did not conform to the regular expression [a-z]+`  Adjust the value to match the schema's pattern, or loosen the pattern.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.5`  `NumberOutOfRange`  A number falls outside the `minimum`/`maximum` (or exclusive bounds) the schema declares. Raised by the `"number!"` provider type.  `[↯/s.106.3.5] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the number was not between -90.0 and 90.0`  Constrain the value to the schema's permitted range.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.6`  `LengthOutOfRange`  A string's length falls outside the schema's `minLength`/`maxLength`. Raised by the `"string!"` provider type.  `[↯/s.106.3.6] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the string's length was not between 1 and 214`  Shorten or lengthen the value to fit the schema.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.7`  `NotPermitted`  A string is not one of the schema's `enum` values (or its `const`). Raised by the `"enum"` provider type.  `[↯/s.106.3.7] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value Polygon was not one of Point`  Use one of the listed values, or extend the schema's `enum`.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.8`  `UnexpectedKind`  A value is of a JSON kind which none of the alternatives of its union (`anyOf`, `oneOf`, or a `type` naming several) accepts.  `[↯/s.106.3.8] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value was a JSON boolean, which is not one of string, number`  Give a value of one of the kinds the schema lists.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.9`  `Unparsable`  A string's text is not valid for its `format`: a `json-pointer` or a `regex` which does not parse.  `[↯/s.106.3.9] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value a[ is not a valid regex`  Correct the value so that it parses in its format.
+ column  Código
+ column  Motivo
+ column  Significado
+ column  Mensaje
+ column  Solución
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.1`  `JsonType`  El tipo del valor no coincide con el que exige el esquema.  `[↯/s.106.3.1] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because expected JSON type number, but found string`  Proporciona un valor del tipo que exige el esquema, o relaja el esquema si el tipo es realmente flexible.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.2`  `MissingValue`  Falta en el JSON un valor obligatorio. El motivo nombra el campo ausente cuando se conoce.  `[↯/s.106.3.2] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value of locality was missing`  Añade el campo que falta, o márcalo como opcional en el esquema.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.3`  `IntOutOfRange`  Un valor entero queda fuera del `minimum`/`maximum` que permite el esquema. Lo lanza el tipo de proveedor `"integer!"`; una cota ausente es `Unset` y no un centinela.  `[↯/s.106.3.3] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value was not between 1 and 99`  Limita el valor al rango que permite el esquema.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.4`  `PatternMismatch`  Un valor de cadena no coincide con la expresión regular del `pattern` del esquema.  `[↯/s.106.3.4] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value did not conform to the regular expression [a-z]+`  Ajusta el valor para que coincida con el patrón del esquema, o relaja el patrón.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.5`  `NumberOutOfRange`  Un número queda fuera del `minimum`/`maximum` (o de las cotas exclusivas) que declara el esquema. Lo lanza el tipo de proveedor `"number!"`.  `[↯/s.106.3.5] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the number was not between -90.0 and 90.0`  Limita el valor al rango que permite el esquema.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.6`  `LengthOutOfRange`  La longitud de una cadena queda fuera del `minLength`/`maxLength` del esquema. Lo lanza el tipo de proveedor `"string!"`.  `[↯/s.106.3.6] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the string's length was not between 1 and 214`  Acorta o alarga el valor para que se ajuste al esquema.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.7`  `NotPermitted`  Una cadena no es uno de los valores del `enum` del esquema (ni su `const`). Lo lanza el tipo de proveedor `"enum"`.  `[↯/s.106.3.7] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value Polygon was not one of Point`  Usa uno de los valores enumerados, o amplía el `enum` del esquema.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.8`  `UnexpectedKind`  Un valor es de una clase JSON que no acepta ninguna de las alternativas de su unión (`anyOf`, `oneOf`, o un `type` que nombra varias).  `[↯/s.106.3.8] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value was a JSON boolean, which is not one of string, number`  Da un valor de una de las clases que enumera el esquema.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.9`  `Unparsable`  El texto de una cadena no es válido para su `format`: un `json-pointer` o una `regex` que no se puede analizar.  `[↯/s.106.3.9] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value a[ is not a valid regex`  Corrige el valor para que se pueda analizar en su formato.

